-- title:
--   End leading residues and χ_U(0) on a crossing model
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation domain (a discrete valuation ring that is a domain and is adically complete for its maximal ideal), let $\varpi \in W$ be irreducible and let $e \ge 1$. Write $R =$ `UVCrossingModel W (ϖ ^ e)`, the quotient of the two-variable power series ring `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) W` by the ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - \varpi^{e}$. Let $x \in R$ be nonzero, and let $ab = (a,b)$ be a pair of one-variable power series over $W$ with $b$ of zero constant term such that the class of `inU a + inV b` (the two-variable series whose coefficients along $d_1 = 0$ are those of $a$, plus the one whose coefficients along $d_0 = 0$ are those of $b$) equals $x$; assume some coefficient of $a$ is a unit, and that either the constant coefficient of $a$ is a unit or some coefficient $b_j$ with $j \ge 1$ is a unit. Assume $R/xR$ is finite and free as a $W$-module, and that its rank equals $\inf D_0 - \sup D_e$, where $D_t =$ `dominantIndices (IsDiscreteValuationRing.addVal W) e t ab` is the set of $n \in \mathbb{Z}$ at which `termOrder`, namely $\mathrm{addVal}_W(\mathrm{nfCoeff}\,ab\,n) + \mathrm{annulusWeight}\,e\,t\,(\mathrm{nfExponent}\,n)$, attains the value `repGaussOrder`, the infimum over all multi-exponents $d$ of $\mathrm{addVal}_W$ of the $d$-th coefficient of `inU a + inV b` plus $\mathrm{annulusWeight}\,e\,t\,d$; here $\mathrm{nfCoeff}\,ab\,n$ is $a_n$ for $n \ge 0$ and $b_{j+1}$ for $n = -(j+1)$. Then, with `leadingResidue ϖ c` the residue in the residue field of $W$ of the unit part of $c$ (and $0$ when $c = 0$), the leading residue of the constant coefficient of the characteristic polynomial of the $W$-linear endomorphism of $R/xR$ given by multiplication by the image of `U (ϖ ^ e)`, times the leading residue of $\mathrm{nfCoeff}\,ab\,(\inf D_0)$, equals the leading residue of $\mathrm{nfCoeff}\,ab\,(\sup D_e)$.
--
--   This is the end-ratio reciprocity for the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV - \varpi^{e})$ of a modular curve at a singular point of its special fibre: the constant term of the characteristic polynomial of multiplication by $U$ on $R/xR$ interpolates, in leading residues, between the extreme normal-form coefficients of $x$ at depths $0$ and $e$. It is used in the computation of residues of norms of the crossing coordinates, feeding the statement `leadingResidue_nfCoeff_sSup_mul_finprod_residue_unitPart_norm_pow_eq_of_isUnit_coeff`.
